{"When fifteen minutes have passed and the bogus DPW truck hasn’t returned, Billy decides they have either moved on to another part of the city, maybe to check out the house on Evergreen Street, or have gone back to the McMansion to await further orders from Nick. He closes the curtain, shutting out the view, and looks at his watch. \003It’s twenty to eleven\004. How time flies when you’re having fun, he thinks.","Billy Summers","Stephen King",true},
{"The station clock told him the time: \003twenty to eleven\004. He went to the booking office and asked the clerk in a polite tone when was the next train to Paris. “In twelve minutes.”","The Man Who Watched the Trains Go By","Georges Simenon",true},
